---
// Generated by packages/calibration-lab/lab/figures.py from results.json. Do not edit by hand.
interface Props { caption?: boolean }
const { caption = true } = Astro.props;
---

<figure>
  <svg class="fig" viewBox="0 0 660 380" role="img" aria-label="Each model plotted by resolution against reliability.">
    <line x1="66.0" y1="30" x2="66.0" y2="332" class="grid" />
    <text x="66.0" y="352" class="tick mid">0.000</text>
    <line x1="204.5" y1="30" x2="204.5" y2="332" class="grid" />
    <text x="204.5" y="352" class="tick mid">0.034</text>
    <line x1="343.0" y1="30" x2="343.0" y2="332" class="grid" />
    <text x="343.0" y="352" class="tick mid">0.068</text>
    <line x1="481.5" y1="30" x2="481.5" y2="332" class="grid" />
    <text x="481.5" y="352" class="tick mid">0.102</text>
    <line x1="620.0" y1="30" x2="620.0" y2="332" class="grid" />
    <text x="620.0" y="352" class="tick mid">0.136</text>
    <line x1="66" y1="332.0" x2="620" y2="332.0" class="grid" />
    <text x="56" y="336.0" class="tick end">0.000</text>
    <line x1="66" y1="256.64" x2="620" y2="256.64" class="grid" />
    <text x="56" y="260.64" class="tick end">0.011</text>
    <line x1="66" y1="181.27" x2="620" y2="181.27" class="grid" />
    <text x="56" y="185.27" class="tick end">0.022</text>
    <line x1="66" y1="105.22" x2="620" y2="105.22" class="grid" />
    <text x="56" y="109.22" class="tick end">0.033</text>
    <line x1="66" y1="29.86" x2="620" y2="29.86" class="grid" />
    <text x="56" y="33.86" class="tick end">0.044</text>
    <line x1="66" y1="332" x2="620" y2="332" class="axis" />
    <line x1="66" y1="30" x2="66" y2="332" class="axis" />
    <text x="343.0" y="372" class="label mid">resolution: how much it knows</text>
    <text x="14" y="181.0" class="label mid" transform="rotate(-90 14 181.0)">reliability: how dishonest</text>
    <circle cx="96.98" cy="329.8" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>keyword rates: reliability 0.0003, resolution 0.0076, AUC 0.608</title></circle>
    <text x="104.98" y="323.8" class="note">keyword rates</text>
    <circle cx="418.88" cy="69.39" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-rose)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>naive Bayes: reliability 0.0383, resolution 0.0866, AUC 0.850</title></circle>
    <text x="426.88" y="63.39" class="note">naive Bayes</text>
    <circle cx="496.3" cy="328.57" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>TF-IDF + LR: reliability 0.0005, resolution 0.1056, AUC 0.872</title></circle>
    <text x="504.3" y="322.57" class="note">TF-IDF + LR</text>
    <circle cx="472.03" cy="323.82" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>TF-IDF + GBM: reliability 0.0012, resolution 0.0997, AUC 0.863</title></circle>
    <text x="480.03" y="337.82" class="note">TF-IDF + GBM</text>
    <circle cx="500.79" cy="328.18" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>probe: reliability 0.0006, resolution 0.1067, AUC 0.874</title></circle>
    <text x="508.79" y="322.18" class="note">probe</text>
    <circle cx="495.37" cy="312.88" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>probe, no L2: reliability 0.0028, resolution 0.1054, AUC 0.871</title></circle>
    <text x="503.37" y="306.88" class="note">probe, no L2</text>
    <circle cx="501.32" cy="317.33" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>MLP head: reliability 0.0021, resolution 0.1069, AUC 0.870</title></circle>
    <text x="509.32" y="331.33" class="note">MLP head</text>
    <circle cx="506.65" cy="308.47" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>Jev (mock): reliability 0.0034, resolution 0.1082, AUC 0.873</title></circle>
    <text x="514.65" y="302.47" class="note">Jev (mock)</text>
    <circle cx="546.21" cy="328.66" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-blue)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>oracle: reliability 0.0005, resolution 0.1179, AUC 0.891</title></circle>
    <text x="554.21" y="322.66" class="note">oracle</text>
  </svg>
  {caption && <figcaption>Murphy&#x27;s split of the Brier score puts every model on two independent axes. Keyword rates are honest and nearly useless; naive Bayes knows a lot and lies about it (reliability 0.038). Down and to the right is better.</figcaption>}
</figure>

<style>
  .fig { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin: 1.6rem auto 0.6rem; }
  .fig text { font-family: var(--font-jetbrains); fill: var(--text-dim); }
  .fig .tick { font-size: 11px; }
  .fig .label { font-size: 11.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .fig .mid { text-anchor: middle; }
  .fig .end { text-anchor: end; }
  .fig .grid { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .fig .axis { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .fig .ref { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-dasharray: 4 4; fill: none; }
  .fig .series { fill: none; stroke-width: 2; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .fig .key { font-size: 11.5px; fill: var(--text); }
  .fig .note { font-size: 11px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .fig .big { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text); }
  figcaption {
    font-family: var(--font-jetbrains);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: 0 auto 2.2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
